Fix empty document windows opened from the home screen

Tauri v2 runs non-async commands on the main thread, so creating a
WebviewWindow inside new_document/open_document deadlocked the event
loop on Windows (wry#583): the window shell appeared but stayed at
about:blank. Mark all commands #[tauri::command(async)] and spawn
worker threads for window creation from main-thread contexts (menu
events, single-instance callback, macOS Reopen/Opened).

Also seed card "1" for new documents in Electron.elm — the current
defaultTree is empty because the web app creates the first card via
the database flow — and load files without <gingko-card> tags (plain
markdown) as a single card instead of an empty tree.

